    {
      "id": "text-94",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 980,
      "width": 1794.1000000000001,
      "height": 122.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 744386,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9844526,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\nThe tree is servers, then databases (SHOW DATABASES), then tables, in a 300px column, or a third of the width if smaller, that scrolls on its own. The grid shows the first 200 rows ('The first 200 rows'), numbered, with NULL in muted\ntext; queries run over SSH on the server's mysql client.\nThe Database tab has no header picker of its own, and the code does not set a subtitle for it. I assume the header keeps the generic project line; I did not confirm this.\nTree notes: 'Connecting…', 'No databases.', 'Loading tables…', 'No tables.', and 'No database login is stored for this server. Add one to it under ⚙ Settings → SSH servers.' The empty grid says 'No table selected — Click a\nserver on the left to see its databases…'.\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "originalText": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\nThe tree is servers, then databases (SHOW DATABASES), then tables, in a 300px column, or a third of the width if smaller, that scrolls on its own. The grid shows the first 200 rows ('The first 200 rows'), numbered, with NULL in muted\ntext; queries run over SSH on the server's mysql client.\nThe Database tab has no header picker of its own, and the code does not set a subtitle for it. I assume the header keeps the generic project line; I did not confirm this.\nTree notes: 'Connecting…', 'No databases.', 'Loading tables…', 'No tables.', and 'No database login is stored for this server. Add one to it under ⚙ Settings → SSH servers.' The empty grid says 'No table selected — Click a\nserver on the left to see its databases…'.\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
  ],
  "appState": {
    "viewBackgroundColor": "#ffffff",
    "gridSize": null
  },
